From: =?UTF-8?q?Ond=C5=99ej=20=C5=A0imon?= <ondrej@dorhawk.software>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:08:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Keep the icon of a program's own bundle in the
 Dock.

A launcher that starts a program from a bundle of its own with an icon
may draw that icon as it wants the program shown: Gentes puts each
app's Windows icon on a tile in the app's own tint. winemac replaced
it with the executable's icon when the first window appeared, so the
Dock showed the bare Windows icon. With CFBundleIconFile pointing at
an image the bundle holds, the application icon is left as the
bundle's; without one, as before.

Measured with Enterprise Architect 17.2 through Gentes: the bundle's
tinted icon stays; before, the owner saw the bare EA icon in the Dock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
index af8be4857e..0f4034b883 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -1151,6 +1151,14 @@ - (void) setCursorWithFrames:(NSArray*)frames
     - (void) setApplicationIconFromCGImageArray:(NSArray*)images
     {
         NSImage* nsimage = nil;
+        NSBundle* bundle = [NSBundle mainBundle];
+        NSString* iconFile = [bundle objectForInfoDictionaryKey:@"CFBundleIconFile"];
+
+        /* A program started from a bundle of its own with an icon (a launcher's, which may draw the
+         * program's icon as it wants it in the Dock) keeps that icon: the default image is the
+         * bundle's. */
+        if ([iconFile isKindOfClass:[NSString class]] && [bundle pathForImageResource:iconFile])
+            images = nil;
 
         if ([images count])
         {
